# SUBJECT evaluation plan

Status: DRAFT — task-specific cases, oracle and environment are not complete.
Mode: MODE. This supplement does not replace the original 99-rule ledger.

## Complete the target-specific inputs

1. Adapt `evals/routing.json.template` into `evals/routing.json`: replace every
   REPLACE value with domain prompts, negative boundaries and label rationales.
   Keep a fixed development/validation split; do not copy builder-evaluation prompts.
2. Adapt `evals/execution.json.template` into `evals/execution.json`: define normal,
   boundary, missing-capability and hostile-input cases as relevant. Give each
   check/invariant a concrete independent oracle here before running trials.
   Fixture paths are relative to one explicitly approved fixture root.
3. Adapt `evals/environment.json.template` into `evals/environment.json`.
   Freeze host/model/settings/tools/catalog, allowed effects and budget. Choose
   the budget for this task; template numbers are editable defaults, not a standard.
4. Record the baseline task failures or expertise being captured, why a skill
   is appropriate, and what parsing/verification belongs in deterministic code.
   Measure actual loaded context before pruning; KB byte counts are not tokens.
5. Adapt `workflow-contract.json.template`: give output/required/forbidden
   requirements stable IDs, owner paths/digests and case/check mappings. Run the
   installed `scripts/review.py contract` against the subject root and execution
   cases. Forbidden actions map to invariants. A valid map is not semantic proof.
6. Adapt observable `trajectory` rules to domain actions; do not copy example
   names as if the subject emitted them. Record action success/failure/denial in
   independent traces. Check only meaningful order; equivalent workflows remain valid.
7. Include redacted field incidents and human annotations with source identity.
   Keep synthetic fixtures labeled. Retain affected versions, failed attempts
   and the owning-layer fix in `papercut.json.template`; close only with an
   independent identity-bound regression receipt. Reports remain local.
8. Review numbered steps using `scripts/review.py lint`; resolve or explain the
   advisory locations through semantic review. Use `ABLATION-PLAN.md` when
   testing instruction variants, and consider retirement when evidence warrants it.

